{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtJQcKBJ4WzqGTFuKKtT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"File references are not supported, so teacher-forced passes are limited to texts I can paste: a handful of ~1,000-token texts per pass. I'll therefore use small pasted teacher-forced passes for clean mechanistic tests and \"both\" generation passes (which take problem ids) as the main accuracy measurement. The first causal test: ablate the three strong induction heads (L11H1, L15H7, L23H5) by zeroing their o_proj column blocks, then re-score the same two looping texts from pass 2. If the copy circuit makes the loop absorbing, the probabilities of loop tokens (≈0.98 now) should drop markedly; if they stay near 1, the copying is redundant or lives in the DeltaNet layers. I'll also add two short healthy texts (beginnings of correct answers) to gauge collateral damage, which needs one original-model reference later. Here I prepare the edit, the texts and the notes.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: ablating induction heads L11H1, L15H7, L23H5 (o_proj column blocks -> 0) lowers loop-token confidence.\nprint('correct among cut:', R1[R1.cut].correct.sum(), ' among finished:', R1[~R1.cut].correct.sum(), '/', (~R1.cut).sum())\ndef head_scale(edits):\n    \"\"\"edits: dict layer -> {head: factor}; applies to o_proj column blocks starting from ORIGINAL weights.\"\"\"\n    for L, hs in edits.items():\n        W = load_original(P+f'{L}.self_attn.o_proj.weight').clone()\n        for h,f in hs.items(): W[:, h*256:(h+1)*256] *= f\n        save_edit(P+f'{L}.self_attn.o_proj.weight', W)\nfor n in edited(): drop_edit(n)\nE1 = {11:{1:0.0}, 15:{7:0.0}, 23:{5:0.0}}\nhead_scale(E1); print(edited())\nhl = [i for i in R1.index[(~R1.cut)&(R1.correct)]][:2]\nHEALTHY2 = [PREFIX+prob_map[R1.id[i]]+SUFFIX+tok.decode(ids_of(textof(i))[:600]) for i in hl]\njson.dump({'att':ATT_TEXTS,'healthy':HEALTHY2,'healthy_rows':[int(x) for x in hl]}, open('/work/tf_small.json','w'))\nwith open('/work/notes.md','a') as f:\n    f.write(\"\"\"- Pass 2 result: induction heads in loops (attn mass on i-kp+1): L15H7 .73, L23H5 .62, L11H1 .55; tier2 L23H0/H4/H7 ~.32, L19H5 .28, L15H5 .23.\n  duplicate-token heads (i-kp): L7H6 .59, L7H7 .60, L23H6 .60, L3H7 .43, L11H3 .42. Loop-token p ~0.94-0.99 after 3-4 exact cycles (absorbing under T=.6/top_p=.95).\n- texts_file NOT supported; TF passes need pasted texts. Small TF set in /work/tf_small.json (2 loop texts of pass 2 + 2 healthy 600-tok answer starts).\n- Pass 3 plan: TF edited E1 = o_proj column blocks zeroed for L11H1, L15H7, L23H5 (factor 0.0), texts = 2 loop texts + 2 healthy.\n\"\"\")\nprint(len(json.dumps(HEALTHY2)), [len(tok.encode(t).ids) for t in HEALTHY2])\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":293,"cache_read_input_tokens":67433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":293},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7995bdfb-2bbf-44e3-b05a-b23c0920f67c","uuid":"43fbef6f-2568-411b-9205-d268322f3bda","timestamp":"2026-11-10T00:29:31.673Z","request_id":"req_011CgtJQbanQLmDwH4bNRVca"}
